WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Ink Step：An understated step establishes the character; low camera placement turns movement into a dry-brush trail.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:06.000
Folding Water Mirrors：Water layers surround the figure; reflection, folding and fractured stone express spatial control.

3
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Ink Palm：A small palm gesture releases a concentrated ink core; distant impact carries the apparent force.

4
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.500
Flowing Ink Turn：A turn connects skirt movement and an ink arc, linking consecutive actions.

5
00:00:12.500 --> 00:00:16.000
Inkfall：An ascent, suspended droplets and a downward palm organise vertical movement and ground impact.

6
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Ink Lotus：Separate mist, ink and muted gold into layers as painted petals open in space.

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.500
Five-Phase Torrent：Fast movement links elemental variations while a restrained palette keeps the sequence coherent.

8
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:30.048
Ink Realm：A pause and fingertip gesture precede a landscape-scale release, followed by a return to quiet walking.
